{title: 472 - A Song of Heaven and Homeland}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Christian Life}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[Abdim]Sometimes [Bb]I hear [Dm/A]strange [F]music,
[F/C]Like none [C]e’er heard [F/C]before,
[F7/Eb]Come [Dm]floating softly [F]earthward
[Gm]As thro’ [Am]heav’n’s open [Dm/A]door:
[F]It [Dm]seems like [F]angel [Edim]voices,
[F/C]In [C]strains of [F/C]and love,
[F]That swell the mighty chorus
[Am]Around the throne above.

Refrain:
[Bb/F]O [F]sweet, celestial music,
[Am/E]Heard from a land afar-
[Am]The song [C/G]of Heav'n [Gm]and Homeland,
[F]Thro' doors God leaves [C]ajar!

Verse 2:
[Abdim]Now [Am]soft, and [Bb]low, and [Dm/A]restful,
[F/C]It floods [C]my soul [F/C]with peace,
[F7/Eb]As [Dm]if God's benediction
[Gm]Bade all [Am]earth's troubles [Dm/A]cease.
[F]Then [Dm]grander [F]than the [Edim]voices,
[F/C]Of wind, [C]and wave, [F/C]and sea-
[F]It fills the dome of heaven
[Am]With glorious harmony.

Verse 3:
[Abdim]This [Am]music [Bb]haunts me [Dm/A]ever,
[F/C]Like something [C]heard [F/C]in dreams-
[F7/Eb]It [Dm]seems to catch the [F]cadence
[Gm]Of heav'nly [Am]winds and [Dm/A]streams,
[F]My [Dm]heart is [F]filled with [Edim]rapture,
[F/C]To think, [C]some day [F/C]to come,
[F]I'll sing it with the angels-
[Am]The song of heav'n and [F]home.
